#=GF RL Nucleic Acids Res 1990;18:2633-2642.
#=GF CC U6 snRNA is a component of the spliceosome which is involved in splicing
#=GF CC pre-mRNA. The putative secondary structure consensus base pairing is
#=GF CC confined to a short 5' stem loop, but U6 snRNA is thought to form
#=GF CC extensive base-pair interactions with U4 snRNA [2]. This model hits a
#=GF CC large number of sequences in vertebrate genomes, which appear to be U6
#=GF CC derived pseudogenes or repeats. This family has a high significance
#=GF CC threshold to minimise this problem, but many annotated pseudogenes remain.
#=GF WK U6_spliceosomal_RNA
